    "result": "Answer: **8**.\n\nThe electronics dataset is `g2` (per memory, confirmed by dominant `main_cat`). Since `items_g2` has no `rtg_ct` column, both the review count and the average review rating must be derived from `fdbk_g2`. I verified price encoding (`prc` = cents, all overlapping rows match `prc_usd`=prc/100, 0 mismatches) and used `prc > 5000` to cover all priced rows including the 224 that lack `prc_usd`. Note the stored `items_g2.avg_rtg` is wildly inconsistent with the review-derived average (e.g. stored 4.7 vs actual 2.79), so the review aggregate is the correct basis.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": 8,\n  \"sql\": \"SELECT COUNT(*) AS n_products FROM (SELECT i.ref_id FROM items_g2 i JOIN fdbk_g2 f ON f.ref_id = i.ref_id WHERE i.prc > 5000 GROUP BY i.ref_id HAVING COUNT(*) >= 5 AND AVG(f.rtg) < 3.0);\"\n}\n```\n\nThe 8 qualifying products (all confirmed with ≥5 reviews, review-average < 3.0, price > $50): B00AUD1YES, B0027VT6SM, B0000DIXC2, B09F1TKF85, B07SDNZDBL, B07WVF9SL5, B000WGSAAE, B074QNH55H.",
